@startuml SequenceAddTask
title Week 6 Add a Task Through the Builder
actor User
participant "Input and add buttons" as UI
participant "main.js" as Main
participant TodoController as Controller
participant TodoService as Service
participant TaskBuilder as Builder
participant Task
participant LocalStorageHandler as Storage
participant "Browser localStorage" as BrowserStorage
participant TodoRenderer as Renderer
participant "Task container and document" as Page

User -> UI : Enter description and choose an action
alt Add Task or Enter
  UI -> Main : normal click handler
  Main -> Controller : addTask(input.value)
  Controller -> Service : addTask(description)
else Add Urgent
  UI -> Main : urgent click handler
  Main -> Controller : addUrgentTask(input.value)
  Controller -> Service : addUrgentTask(description)
end
Service -> Service : validate(description)

alt Trimmed description has fewer than 3 characters
  Service -> User : alert validation message
  Service --> Controller : null
  Controller --> Main : null
  note over Main, Page : Input and rendered lists remain unchanged
else Valid description
  note right of Service
    validate() returns trimmed text and warns
    if the existing list has at least 20 tasks.
  end note
  Service -> Builder : new TaskBuilder(trimmed)
  opt addUrgentTask() construction
    Service -> Builder : setPriority('high')
    Builder --> Service : this
    Service -> Builder : addLabel('URGENT')
    Builder --> Service : this
  end
  Service -> Builder : build()
  Builder -> Task : new Task(this)
  Task --> Builder : task
  Builder --> Service : task
  note over Service, Builder
    Separate service methods select these construction steps;
    the opt does not represent a task-type conditional in the code.
  end note
  Service -> Service : store(task): append to tasks
  Service -> Storage : save(tasks)
  Storage -> BrowserStorage : setItem('todo-tasks', JSON.stringify(tasks))
  Service --> Controller : task.id
  Controller -> Renderer : render(service, task.id)
  Renderer -> Service : getWorkloadSummary()
  Service --> Renderer : workload text
  Renderer -> Renderer : Read tasks and build both lists
  Renderer -> Page : Update lists, status, and page title
  Renderer -> Page : Bind actions and flash new row
  Controller --> Main : task.id
  Main -> UI : Clear input
end

note over UI, Main : Enter triggers the normal Add Task button.
note over Service, Storage
  StorageFactory.createService() supplied this service's backend at startup.
  With InMemoryStorageFactory, save() updates its array instead of localStorage.
end note
@enduml
